# Milestone: M3
# Covers: ',' separator fire-and-forget; detached strand runs concurrently
#         with main strand; timing interleaving via sleep.
# defer-to: M5 (chk runner needs urbi_step driver path for ',' separator)
#
# Reason:
#   ',' (OP_FORK_DETACH) fires a detached strand.  The chk runner uses the
#   uvm_run REPL path (realm == NULL); OP_FORK_DETACH produces "TypeError:
#   requires urbi_step driver" in that context (see comma_amp_unsupported.chk).
#   Timing-based ordering (sleep interleave) additionally requires the step
#   driver to advance time and schedule strands.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M5 with urbi_step chk driver):
# # 42,
# # {sleep(200ms); echo("bar")}, sleep(100ms); echo("foo");
# # [00000001] *** foo
# # [00000002] *** bar
# # sleep(200ms);
